  "id": "COMPOUND:30036 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 7-Angeloylechinatine may have a potential role in modulating HepG2 cell behavior through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting two distinct proteins: Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is a target of Nudiposide and (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid. Both of these compounds are known to interact with HepG2 cells, indicating a possible downstream effect on cellular processes in the cancer cell line. Additionally, 7-Angeloylechinatine is linked to VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Vidalol B, and Vidalol B is also known to interact with HepG2. This suggests that 7-Angeloylechinatine may exert its effects through a network of targets that ultimately influence HepG2 cell function. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways that are relevant to HepG2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
